   "family": "shes",
   "is_root": true,
   "etymology": "A prefixal derivative in -es, also attested in pres (“to cut, carve”), with original meaning 'to cut off, divide, separate in a share'. The origin of the first component, sh-, is unclear, though has been compared to English sell and thus Proto-Indo-European *selh₁- (“to take”). However, Orel later proposes a different derivation from Proto-Albanian *iš-agtja, from Proto-Indo-European *h₂eǵ- (“to drive”).",
